"""Plain-language Dashboard help, kept independent of Qt.

Definitions checked against Microsoft's Working Set documentation,
https://learn.microsoft.com/windows/win32/memory/working-set,
Private Bytes guidance,
https://learn.microsoft.com/windows-hardware/drivers/debugger/using-performance-monitor-to-find-a-user-mode-memory-leak,
and the GPU engine explanation at
https://devblogs.microsoft.com/directx/gpus-in-the-task-manager/.
The collectors, rather than Task Manager's display conventions, determine units.
"""

READ_ONLY = "Nothing here changes Windows settings. Reading needs no administrator rights; protected information may be unavailable."
PROCESS_ACTIONS = "Process actions can stop programs or change their scheduling; access to other users' processes may need administrator rights. Ending a process cannot recover its unsaved work."

